// 1. Normalise: $x^{\text{lvl}}=(x-x_L)/\sigma$, bridge $b(t)=x_1+(x_L-x_1)\,t$, $x^{\text{br}}=(x-b)/\sigma$. Smooth $s=\text{MA}_{25}(x^{\text{lvl}})$, global residual $r=x^{\text{lvl}}-s$.
// 2. Compute four pred-len projections (per channel, 1/L init):
//    a. local: Linear$(x^{\text{lvl}}_{-L_s:})$ with $L_s=\max(8,L/4)$.
//    b. global: Linear$(r)$.
//    c. bridge: Linear$(x^{\text{br}})$.
//    d. diff: Linear of first differences of the local window.
// 3. Build six per-channel statistics (recent vol, long vol, trend magnitude, mean shift, acceleration, endpoint gap).
// 4. Gate: $\text{softmax}(\text{Linear}_6 \to 3\cdot H)$ → per-step three-branch weights; amplitude $1+0.1\tanh(\text{Linear}_6 \to H)$.
// 5. Anchor mix: $\sigma(1.5(\text{trend\_mag}/\text{long\_vol}-1))$ blends persistence $x_L$ with future bridge.
// 6. $\hat y=(g_0(local+0.5\,diff)+g_1\,global+g_2\,bridge)\cdot\sigma\cdot\text{amp}+\text{anchor}$.
